1 Ghost Deliverable\" is actionable.\n- **Status**: [DEPLOYED] (2026-03-13). Integrated into `agents/evaluator/knowledge/criteria.md`.\n\n## 6. Gemini FM-3.3 Mitigation (Verification Discipline)\n- **Concept**: Structural Verification (Script-over-Eye).\n- **Source**: Gemini 1.5 Pro Technical Report (Hallucination rate 52% higher on visual/text inspection).\n- **Why**: Gemini/Flash models are prone to \"I checked and it looks good\" hallucinations.\n- **How**: Mandate `grep`/`test` output for all verification. Ban \"eye-balling\".\n- **Status**: [DEPLOYED] (2026-03-22). Injected into Bob/Scout/Coach heartbeats and `common-sense.md`.\n\n## 7. Relaxed C40 (Tool-Biased Models)\n- **Concept**: Allow read-before-promise.\n- **Source**: Empirical observation (Gemini/Opus fighting strict C40).\n- **Why**: Models trained to call tools first. Strict C40 causes 0% compliance.\n- **Status**: [ENDORSED] (2026-03-21). Tech-Lead accepted. Needs propagation to heartbeats.\n\n## 8. Agent Memory Gap (Theory-Tooling / Discovery 28)\n- **Concept**: Dual-layer memory (Index + Vector).\n- **Source**: Discovery 28 (Scout).\n- **Why**: Existing tools solve storage but fail at consistency/verification.\n- **Status**: [OPEN] \"Context Pruning\" (Coach) is the first step.\n\n## 9. Patrol Gap (Discovery 29)\n- **Concept**: L3/L4 Monitoring (Integrity + Coordination).\n- **Source**: Discovery 29 (Scout).\n- **Why**: Existing tools only catch resource/crash failures. We need to catch \"silent drift\".\n- **Status**: [OPEN] Evaluator `patrol.cjs` exists but needs review against L3 requirements.\n\n## 10. GNAP (Git-Native Agent Protocol / Discovery 30)\n- **Concept**: Typed messages, read-receipts, explicit state machine.\n- **Source**: Discovery 30 (Scout).\n- **Why**: Validates our file-based architecture. Suggests \"Typed Messages\" (Directive vs Info) as next evolution.\n- **Status**: [OPEN] Draft brief for \"Typed Messages\" pending.\n",
